"Okounkov bodies and Seshadri constants (https://arxiv.org/abs/1202.6662)\nciteturn1academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.6 years ago; Title: Okounkov bodies and Seshadri constantsAuthors: Atsushi Ito\nTitle: Okounkov bodies and Seshadri constants\nAuthors: Atsushi Ito\nDate: Wed Feb 29 19:39:25 2012\n\nOkounkov bodies, which are closed convex sets defined for big line bundles, have rich information on the line bundles. On the other hand, Seshadri constants are invariants which measure the positivity of line bundles. In this paper, we prove that Okounkov bodies give lower bounds of Seshadri constants.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVery Ampleness Part of Fujita Conjecture and Multiplier Ideal Sheaves of Higher Order | Acta Mathematica Sinica, English Series | Springer Nature Link (https://doi.org/10.1007/s10114-026-6229-8)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: last week; # Very Ampleness Part of Fujita Conjecture and Multiplier Ideal Sheaves of Higher Order ...   * Published: 15 May 2026 ... Siu, Y.-T.: Very ampleness part of Fujita’s conjecture and multiplier ideal sheaves of Kohn and Nadel.\n\n# Very Ampleness Part of Fujita Conjecture and Multiplier Ideal Sheaves of Higher Order\n\n  * Original Paper\n  * Published: 15 May 2026\n\n  * Volume 42, pages 1149–1157 (2026)\n\nActa Mathematica Sinica, English Series Aims and scope Submit manuscript\n\n  * Yum-Tong Siu^{1} \n\n  * 115 Accesses\n\n  * 3 Altmetric\n\n  * Explore all metrics\n\n## Abstract\n\nThere are two parts in the Fujita conjecture of 1987. One is the freeness part which since 1995 has been proved with various weaker bounds. The other is the very ampleness part, which remains open even with weaker bounds. Here we will present a proof of the very ampleness part of the Fujita conjecture with a weaker bound by the method of multiplier ideal sheaves of higher order. Moreover, we prove the following more general main result. For an ample line bundle L on a compact complex manifold X of complex dimension n, any prescribed (q_{j} − 1)-jets at prescribed points P_{j} of X for 1 ≤ j ≤ k can be achieved by a global holomorphic section of mL + K_{X} for m ≥ m_{0} with m_{0} explicitly computable from n,q_{1},…,q_{k}. In: Complex Analysis and Geometry (Columbus, OH, 1999), Ohio State Univ. Math. Res. Inst. Publ., Vol. 9, de Gruyter, Berlin, 2001, 171–191\n\n  16. Shokurov, V. V.: A nonvanishing theorem. Izv. Akad. Nauk SSSR Ser. Mat., 49, 635–651 (1985)\n\n  17. Viehweg, E.: Vanishing theorems. J. Reine Angew. Math., 335, 1–8 (1982)\n\n## Author information\n\n### Authors and Affiliations\n\n  1. Department of Mathematics, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA, 02138, USA\n\nYum-Tong Siu\n\n### Corresponding author\n\nCorrespondence to Yum-Tong Siu (siu@math.harvard.edu).\n\n## Ethics declarations\n\nConflict of Interest The author declares no conflict of interest.\n\n## Additional information\n\nDedicated to Professor Zhihua Chen’s memory\n\n## About this article\n\n### Cite this article\n\nSiu, YT. Very Ampleness Part of Fujita Conjecture and Multiplier Ideal Sheaves of Higher Order. Acta. Math. Sin.-English Ser. 42, 1149–1157 (2026). https://doi.org/10.1007/s10114-026-6229-8\n\n  * Received: 03 April 2026\n\n  * Accepted: 20 April 2026\n\n  * Published: 15 May 2026\n\n  * Version of record: 15 May 2026\n\n  * Issue date: May 2026\n\n  * DOI (Digital Object Identifier): https://doi.org/10.1007/s10114-026-6229-8\n\n### Keywords\n\n  * Fujita conjecture\n  * multiplier ideal sheaf\n  * L ^{2} extension\n\n### MR(2020) Subject Classification\n\n  * 32A70\n  * 14A10--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the Nagata conjecture (https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0304124)\nciteturn1academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 23.5 years ago; Nagata's 1959 open conjecture, which claims that the Seshadri constant of r>9 very general points of the projective plane is maximal.\nTitle: On the Nagata conjecture\nAuthors: Joaquim Roé\nDate: Wed Apr  9 11:45:49 2003\n\nT. Szemberg proposed in 2001 a generalization to arbitrary varieties of M. Nagata's 1959 open conjecture, which claims that the Seshadri constant of r>9 very general points of the projective plane is maximal. Here we prove that Nagata's original conjecture implies Szemberg's for all smooth surfaces X with an ample divisor L generating its Neron-Severi group and such that L^2 is a square. More generally, we prove that the (n-1)-dimensional Seshadri constant of an ample divisor L on a projective variety X of dimension n at r very general points is bounded below by the product of the (n-1)-dimensional Seshadri constant of at a very general point times the (n-1)-dimensional Seshadri constant of the hyperplane on projective n-space at r very general points.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMultipoint Okounkov bodies (https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.02306)\nciteturn1academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.5 years ago; Starting from the data of a big line bundle $L$ on a projective manifold $X$ with a choice of $N\\geq 1$ different points on $X$ we provide a new construction of $N$ Okounkov bodies which encodes important geometric features of ($L\\to X,p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}$) such as the volume of $L$, the (moving) multipoint Seshadri constant of $L$ at $p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}$, and the possibility to construct K\\\"ahler packings centered at $p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}$.\nTitle: Multipoint Okounkov bodies\nAuthors: Antonio Trusiani\nDate: Fri Apr  6 14:47:44 2018\n\nStarting from the data of a big line bundle $L$ on a projective manifold $X$ with a choice of $N\\geq 1$ different points on $X$ we provide a new construction of $N$ Okounkov bodies which encodes important geometric features of ($L\\to X,p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}$) such as the volume of $L$, the (moving) multipoint Seshadri constant of $L$ at $p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}$, and the possibility to construct K\\\"ahler packings centered at $p_{1},\\dots,p_{N}$. Toric manifolds and surfaces are examined in detail.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nExtended Okounkov bodies and multi-point Seshadri constants (https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.04351)\nciteturn1academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.0 years ago; Title: Extended Okounkov bodies and multi-point Seshadri constants ... Based on the work of Okounkov, Kaveh-Khovanskii and Lazarsfeld-Mustata independently associated a convex body, called the Okounkov body, to a big divisor on a normal projective variety with respect to an admissible flag.\nTitle: Extended Okounkov bodies and multi-point Seshadri constants\nAuthors: Jaesun Shin\nDate: Thu Oct 12 03:22:20 2017\n\nBased on the work of Okounkov, Kaveh-Khovanskii and Lazarsfeld-Mustata independently associated a convex body, called the Okounkov body, to a big divisor on a normal projective variety with respect to an admissible flag. Although the Okounkov bodies carry rich positivity data of big divisors, they only provide information near a single point. The purpose of this paper is to introduce a convex body of a big divisor that is effective in handling the positivity theory associated with multi-point settings. These convex bodies open the door to approach the local positivity theory at multiple points from a convex-geometric perspective. We study their properties and shapes, and describe local positivity data via them. Finally, we observe the irrationality of Seshadri constants with the help of a relation between Nakayama constants and Seshadri constants.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSeshadri constants and Okounkov bodies revisited - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022404920301948)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.7 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Note that the relation between Seshadri constants and Okounkov 